<title>SWEDEN: Reuters' eighth ex-Stockholm air cargo report.</title>
<headline>Reuters' eighth ex-Stockholm air cargo report.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the currency average ex-Stockholm air cargo market rates per kg in Swedish crowns for a 100 kg shipment, with a volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-one:</p>
<p>					    March 18	Jan 13</p>
<p>		 UNITED STATES</p>
<p> STO-JFK				  10.00	    10.00</p>
<p> STO-CHI				  11.30	    11.20</p>
<p> STO-LAX				  12.90	    12.70</p>
<p>		 ASIA-PACIFIC</p>
<p> STO-HKG				  13.50	    13.40</p>
<p> STO-SIN				  13.60	    13.50</p>
<p> STO-NRT				  19.85	    19.65</p>
<p> STO-BKK				  13.10	    13.10</p>
<p>		 MIDDLE EAST</p>
<p> STO-DXB				  10.00	    10.20</p>
<p>		    AFRICA</p>
<p> STO-JNB				  20.10	    20.30</p>
<p>		    EUROPE</p>
<p> STO-LON				   7.45	     7.55</p>
<p> STO-PAR				   7.25	     7.25</p>
<p>		    LATIN AMERICA</p>
<p> STO-SAO				  20.70	    20.80</p>
<p>*The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters journalists on a confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents based at Stockholm's international Arlanda airport.</p>
<p>*All prices quoted in Swedish crowns.</p>
<p>*The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices and are indicative or current market activity.</p>
<p>-- Air Cargo newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
